  "text": "Your groups\n\nThis page is yours, and only this computer opens it: nobody in your groups sees it. Here you see your groups and who in them is on now, open what they lend you, invite people, and lend what runs on this computer.\n\nA link you make works for a day, while this computer is on. When you make a new one, your last one lets nobody new in; everyone it let in stays.\n\nA program on this computer, such as a chat app, can use what is lent to you too: press “Copy its address for a program” beside it, then paste that where the program asks for an address.\n\nA group whose name this computer cannot read\nada\non now\nbo\non now\n\nShow this group on a screen\n\nMake a link to invite someone to this groupMake a link to add your phone or another computer of yoursHave a guest\n\nYou keep the order of removals in this group. Choose who keeps it after you, then leave: \nbo\nHand it on\n\nLeaving this group stops it reaching you, and stops what you lend reaching its people. What you have of it stays on this computer, its folder too. Rejoining needs a new invitation, and this computer can’t rejoin yet. Leave this group\n\nWhat\tWhat it is\tWhose\tHow it opens\tNow\nNobody lends anything here yet.\nBring things to the table\n\nThese come with svrngs. Bring one, and everyone in your group opens it on their own computer or phone, while any computer in your group is on.\n\n Money: who paid for what, and who owes whom.\n\n Events: post a get-together, and see who’s coming.\n\n House rules: the rules your house agrees, and how you agree them.\n\nBring the ticked ones to your group\n\nOpen a link from your group\n\nThe link: Open it\n\nMake a group\n\nA name for the group: Your name in it: Make a group\n\nJoin a group from a link\n\nThe link someone sent you: Your name in it: \n\nAlready running here\n\nYou looked just now: the programs running on this computer, each at its address. Lend one, and everyone in your groups opens it in their browser, as themselves, while this computer is on. You can stop lending it below at any time.\n\nLook for programs running on this computer\n\nSomething at http://localhost:2222. To lend it, give it a name and say what it is, each one word; if it is llama-server, say that. Its name: What it is: Lend it to everyone in your groups\nSomething at http://localhost:2223. To lend it, give it a name and say what it is, each one word; if it is llama-server, say that. Its name: What it is: Lend it to everyone in your groups\nSomething at http://localhost:4226. To lend it, give it a name and say what it is, each one word; if it is llama-server, say that. Its name: What it is: Lend it to everyone in your groups\nSomething at http://localhost:5000. To lend it, give it a name and say what it is, each one word; if it is llama-server, say that. Its name: What it is: Lend it to everyone in your groups\nSomething at http://localhost:7000. To lend it, give it a name and say what it is, each one word; if it is llama-server, say that. Its name: What it is: Lend it to everyone in your groups\nYou lent jellyfin, at http://localhost:8096: everyone in your groups can open it now. It keeps its own accounts, so make each person one in it: your picture at the top right, then Dashboard, Users and +; give it a name and a password, tick the libraries they may watch, and Save.\nSomething at http://localhost:9741. To lend it, give it a name and say what it is, each one word; if it is llama-server, say that. Its name: What it is: Lend it to everyone in your groups\nSomething at http://localhost:9742. To lend it, give it a name and say what it is, each one word; if it is llama-server, say that. Its name: What it is: Lend it to everyone in your groups\nSomething at http://localhost:9743. To lend it, give it a name and say what it is, each one word; if it is llama-server, say that. Its name: What it is: Lend it to everyone in your groups\nSomething at http://localhost:9747. To lend it, give it a name and say what it is, each one word; if it is llama-server, say that. Its name: What it is: Lend it to everyone in your groups\nSomething at http://localhost:9748. To lend it, give it a name and say what it is, each one word; if it is llama-server, say that. Its name: What it is: Lend it to everyone in your groups\nSomething at http://localhost:10606. To lend it, give it a name and say what it is, each one word; if it is llama-server, say that. Its name: What it is: Lend it to everyone in your groups\nSomething at http://localhost:19348. To lend it, give it a name and say what it is, each one word; if it is llama-server, say that. Its name: What it is: Lend it to everyone in your groups\nYou lent chores, at http://localhost:20000: everyone in your groups can open it now.\nSomething at http://localhost:20571. To lend it, give it a name and say what it is, each one word; if it is llama-server, say that. Its name: What it is: Lend it to everyone in your groups\nSomething at http://localhost:20968. To lend it, give it a name and say what it is, each one word; if it is llama-server, say that. Its name: What it is: Lend it to everyone in your groups\nSomething at http://localhost:22644. To lend it, give it a name and say what it is, each one word; if it is llama-server, say that. Its name: What it is: Lend it to everyone in your groups\nSomething at http://localhost:25062. To lend it, give it a name and say what it is, each one word; if it is llama-server, say that. Its name: What it is: Lend it to everyone in your groups\nSomething at http://localhost:26738. To lend it, give it a name and say what it is, each one word; if it is llama-server, say that. Its name: What it is: Lend it to everyone in your groups\nSomething at http://localhost:27234. To lend it, give it a name and say what it is, each one word; if it is llama-server, say that. Its name: What it is: Lend it to everyone in your groups\nSomething at http://localhost:27297. To lend it, give it a name and say what it is, each one word; if it is l